<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS - Australia bank limits should be eased - ACCC.</title>
<headline>RTRS - Australia bank limits should be eased - ACCC.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Competition and Consumer Commission chairman Allan Fels said on Thursday that restrictions on share ownership of banks and foreign ownership of banks needed to be lifted.</p>
<p>Fels said the current restrictions were inconsistent with the commission's in principle stand that any anti-competitive legislation affecting the financial services sector should be repealed unless justified on public-interest grounds.</p>
<p>&quot;Special restrictions on bank ownership and foreign ownership would seem to need to be lifted,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
